      "body": "Drew's standing rule (2026-11-05 01:10 CST): no provider integration may depend on a browser cookie/session that silently expires. Every browser-dependent auth must have (a) an auto-renewing long-lived token, or (b) built-in cookie auto-renewal (automatic re-capture/refresh, e.g. via CDP against the standing signed-in laptop Helium profile, on cadence and on auth failure), with an alert BEFORE hard expiry when renewal fails. Manual re-import steps and one-shot fix-it crons are not an end state.\n\nLANDED with this issue's opening pass:\n- OpenDesign session keeper in the quota gatherer (pm-stack aggregator src/opendesign-renewal.ts): per-tick session read (the Better Auth session slides — verified live 2026-11-05: expiresAt = read-time + 7 days), horizon recorded in ~/.local/state/pm-aggregator/opendesign-renewal.json, CDP re-capture from the laptop Helium with validate-before-store when the stored session fails or runs low, and an alert state while days remain when renewal cannot complete. The one-shot opendesign-cookie-reimport-nov5 cron is retired once the keeper verified live.\n\nREMAINING GAPS (each is follow-through under the rule, not a new decision):\n1. Meta portal fetcher (#6079): the auto-renewal requirement is recorded on that issue (comment 6652154440) — the restore must ship with CDP cookie re-capture + pre-expiry alert built in, not a manual capture step.\n2. Mistral console credits leg (openchamber#1630): /api/billing/credits is cookie-only (both API keys 401). If the usage producer lands on that leg, it needs the same CDP re-capture pattern as the OpenDesign keeper. The plan leg (whoami / account-context) is key-authed and needs no browser.\n3. OpenDesign browser re-arm: the laptop Helium profile currently holds NO Open Design session (verified 2026-11-05 — the profile cookie DB has no open-design rows; the Oct 29 import's session lived in a profile state that did not survive). The keeper's capture leg therefore cannot renew from the browser until someone signs into Open Design in that profile once (Google SSO click-through — proven agent-doable 2026-10-29, no Drew-only step hit then). Until re-armed, renewal-by-use (sliding session, ~7d horizon, checked every 15-min tick) is the live mechanism and the keeper alerts with days of lead if it degrades.\n4. Claude Code leaf credential: ~/.claude/.credentials.json holds an OAuth pair whose refreshTokenExpiresAt is 2026-11-09T06:27Z. Renewal is the CLI's built-in refresh — automatic when the CLI runs — but the claude-code provider is disabled in config, so nothing runs it; if the refresh token lapses, re-login is Drew-only (interactive OAuth). Surface before 2026-11-09 if the provider is to be re-enabled. Side observation: the gatherer's recorded credentialExpiresAt for claude (2026-11-05T14:31:57Z) reads +8h against the file's expiresAt (06:31:57Z, same minutes/seconds/ms) — check the lib's normalizeTimestamp for an offset bug before relying on it for alert lead times.\n5. ClinePass native adapter (dormant — CLINEPASS_CREDENTIAL_REF unset on the laptop gatherer unit): its dashboard token is session-class by design (401/403 = session-expired + needsRelogin in src/clinepass-adapter.ts). Do not enable it without a renewal story. The live module read uses the ClinePass API key and is unaffected.\n6. Alert surfacing: the OpenDesign keeper's alert today is its state file + the gatherer journal. Surface renewal alerts (opendesign-renewal.json status=attention, and equivalents as other providers gain keepers) on the aggregator board / morning readout so a failing renewal is seen without reading state files.\n\nFull inventory: provider-quota-registry.md (auth inventory section, 2026-11-05) and ~/memory/topics/provider-auth-renewal-2026-11-05.md.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Meta portal fetcher (#6079) ships with CDP cookie re-capture + pre-expiry alert built in — no manual capture step.\n- [ ] The Mistral console credits leg (openchamber#1630), if used, has the same CDP re-capture pattern; the key-authed plan leg needs no browser path.\n- [ ] The OpenDesign browser re-arm gap is closed: the laptop Helium profile holds a live Open Design session the keeper can slide/renew, or the keeper's alert fires before hard expiry.\n- [ ] Every browser-dependent provider auth in the fleet has (a) an auto-renewing long-lived token or (b) built-in cookie auto-renewal with a pre-expiry alert — an inventory on this issue proves none is left on manual re-import.\n",
